{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790592477,"nonce":"AlXonDN+tgkuBcOtyvOzlXj5n3w=","title":"Build-script output piles up in target/debug/build across rebuilds","message":"On 2026-09-28 caribou's target/ had grown to 269 GB, 216 GB of it in target/debug/build: caribou-interop 79 GB, wren_lift 28 GB, caribou-plugin-fixtures 25 GB, caribou-driver 21 GB, caribou-runtime 8 GB. Each rebuild whose build-script inputs changed leaves a new OUT_DIR beside the old ones, and these build scripts put whole builds in OUT_DIR (the driver's wasm runtime object, the interop fixtures, the plugin fixtures), so a day of rebuilding the driver fills the disk. Removing target/*/build and target/*/incremental freed it. Worth giving those nested builds a stable target directory of their own (keyed by target triple, not by the build script's hash), so a rebuild reuses and replaces rather than adding.","files":null}]}